    "note": "Mega Delphox surfs its flaming broom (Z-A art: it rides the big branch, the two small brooms fly the same way beside it). It stands across the broom like a surfboard, feet on the stick, knees soft, lead arm out ahead for balance, head turned toward travel. One driver: the board and rider crest a slow swell, one per 3.6 s loop, nose up while rising, banking a little. The knees absorb it (hips dip just after the trough), chest, head and arms follow a beat later; robe tail, sleeves, ear strands and beard trail most; the two small brooms ride the same swell a beat and a half behind; flames lick."
